;
; passenger-side-chamfer.ngc - chamfer the edges of the high part of the
; passenger's side fixture plate.
;
; Copyright (C) 2026 narrativecollapse.  Free software under the WTFPL,
; version 2, with no warranty: see LICENSE.
;
; Run this after passenger-side-plate.ngc and after the 10 degree edge is
; cut on the -Y side (plate-angle.ngc).  Same work holding and datums as
; passenger-side-plate.ngc: X0 Y0 at the top right corner, Z0 on top.
;
; The tool is a 90 degree drill-mill.  Its tip runs #<depth> below the top
; surface and #<offset> outside each edge, so the chamfer is
; #<depth> - #<offset> wide.  Cutter compensation with a "diameter" of
; twice the offset keeps the tip exactly that far from the real outline,
; including around the corners, so the program can follow the outline
; itself.  It goes clockwise, which is climb milling on an outside edge.
;


; -- settings ---------------------------------------------------------

#<clear_z> = 0.500

#<tool> = 4             ; 0.250 90 degree drill-mill
#<tool_dia> = 0.250
#<rpm> = 3000
#<feed> = 3

#<depth> = 0.020
#<offset> = 0.010

; the high part: X-2.750 to X0, Y-2.500 to Y0, with the 10 degree edge
; starting at X-2.101 on the bottom edge
#<wall_x> = -2.750
#<bevel_x> = -2.101
#<bevel_y> = [-2.500 + [#<bevel_x> - #<wall_x>] * TAN[10]]


; -- program ----------------------------------------------------------

o<ar15-start> call [#<clear_z>]
o<ar15-tool> call [#<tool>] [#<rpm>] [#<feed>] [#<tool_dia>]

; start up and to the left of the top left corner, over the thinned area
o<ar15-goto> call [#<wall_x> - 0.250] [0.250]
g41.1 d[2 * #<offset>]
g0 x#<wall_x> y0.000            ; entry move
g1 z[0.000 - #<depth>]

g1 x0.000                       ; top edge
g1 y-2.500                      ; right edge
g1 x#<bevel_x>                  ; bottom edge
g1 x#<wall_x> y#<bevel_y>       ; the 10 degree edge
g1 y0.000                       ; the X-2.750 wall, up through the slots

g0 z#<clear_z>
g40

o<ar15-end> call
m2
